tly divided into 32 shards, each responsible for a portion of the network's total transaction load. This allows for parallel processing and increased scalability.", "before_ok": false, "after_ok": false}, {"prompt": "Q: What is the on-call alias for Juniper?", "expected": "juniper-pager", "before": "The on-call alias for Juniper is \"juniper\".", "after": "The standard pager number is 866-332-2263, and the message format is “*<number> <message>”. If you’re on‑call, you’ll see the text on your phone or via the “show alert‑log” CLI. If you’re not, you can still get the same information by querying the device – for example: …\"", "before_ok": false, "after_ok": false}, {"prompt": "Q: Which region hosts the Wren archive?", "expected": "Mumbai", "before": "The Wren archive is hosted in the \"Wren\" region.", "after": "The WRF community hosts the archive on the University of Wisconsin–Madison’s web server: https://www.earthsystemdynamics.org/wrf/wrf-4.2.0-archive/ (or the equivalent “https://github.com/wrf-model/WRF” for the source code).", "before_ok": false, "after_ok": false}]}
